> How does one bury an iron ball in a pit to get rid of it?

Push a boulder next to the pit. 
Pick up the ball. 
Step into the pit with it.
Drop the ball. 
Crawl out of the pit. Take care not to move too far away from the pit;
stay right next to it as much as you can.
Walk around the boulder.
Push the boulder into the pit.

It may take a few tries (the ball tends to drag along behind you) but
eventually the boulder will be on top of the ball and the iron chain
will snap (= disappear).

   Raisse, killed by a boulder

